time", "call_id": "toolu_01HwBgWhP2e1EmXEBFPigJfh", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53503, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HwBgWhP2e1EmXEBFPigJfh", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 54575, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DUxxQXqiqDCrcsLL9KxqqW", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 54875, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DUxxQXqiqDCrcsLL9KxqqW", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 54875, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DUxxQXqiqDCrcsLL9KxqqW", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59796, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The deploy history shows v2.3.0 is the latest healthy release. The v2.3.1 release and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both marked unhealthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again. The second attempt completed in all three regions.\n- Current status: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, passing health checks. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit a second one and page on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and the retry) and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 is failing, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019xdU9UWqDm1BSmRFqrYQDn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RRmD6phcaF5G8M75Xetxrz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_019vHfawPTVv7jXhqeZNitv8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018PDTnJAtDrCqMCUdoKGUqZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway: us-east is now on v2.3.0, and us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version can safely be repeated, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01SSHeQYTW7mjzr141Li5dAY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RANTRrVyQgFazupdWALjbN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01N5kgNkXFKVwVxww8Z6ZZLX", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01HwBgWhP2e1EmXEBFPigJfh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed (orchestrator error after us-east, leaving the service on mixed versions); a retry finished the rollback in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DUxxQXqiqDCrcsLL9KxqqW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident INC-0001.\n\n**Rollback**\n- The deploy history shows v2.3.0 is the latest healthy release. The v2.3.1 release and its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) were both marked unhealthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- Rolling back to a fixed version is safe to repeat, so I ran it again. The second attempt completed in all three regions.\n- Current status: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, passing health checks. The error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't submit a second one and page on-call twice.\n- INC-0001 is open as SEV2 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the partial failure and the retry) and the current state.\n- It lists two follow-ups: find out why v2.3.1 is failing, and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}